.TH SYOSETU2EPUB 1 "2026-04-18" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
syosetu2epub \- scrape a novel from ncode.syosetu.com and send it to Kindle as an EPUB
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syosetu2epub
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fINOVEL\fR
.br
.B syosetu2epub
.B \-\-setup
.br
.B syosetu2epub
.B \-\-resend
\fIEPUB_PATH\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B syosetu2epub
fetches a novel from ncode.syosetu.com, converts it to a Kindle-ready EPUB, and
emails it to your configured Kindle address by default.
Pass
.B \-\-local
to save the EPUB file locally instead of sending it.
.PP
\fINOVEL\fR may be a bare novel code (e.g.\& \fIn4395il\fR) or a full URL
(e.g.\& \fIhttps://ncode.syosetu.com/n4395il/\fR).
.PP
Scraped chapters are cached under
.I ~/.cache/syosetu2epub/
so subsequent runs do not re-hit the server.
SMTP credentials are stored in
.I ~/.config/syosetu2epub/config.json
after running
.BR \-\-setup .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-setup
Run the interactive credential setup wizard and exit.
Saves Gmail SMTP credentials and an optional default Kindle address to the config file.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH" ", " \-o " PATH"
Write the EPUB to \fIPATH\fR instead of the default \fI<title>.epub\fR in the current directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-chapters " RANGE" ", " \-c " RANGE"
Fetch only a subset of chapters.
\fIRANGE\fR is either a single chapter number (\fI5\fR) or an inclusive range (\fI1\-20\fR).
Chapter numbers are 1-based.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-delay
Skip the 1-second polite delay between HTTP requests.
Speeds up fetching significantly for large novels.
Use sparingly — the delay exists to avoid hammering the server.
.TP
.B \-\-local
Save the EPUB locally and skip sending it to Kindle.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Ignore the local cache and re-download everything from the site.
.TP
.BI \-\-resend " EPUB_PATH"
Skip scraping; attach \fIEPUB_PATH\fR and email it to Kindle directly.
Requires a Kindle address to be configured or passed via \fB\-\-send\-to\fR.
.SS "Send to Kindle"
.TP
.BI \-\-send\-to " KINDLE_EMAIL"
Override the Kindle address from the config file for this run. May be repeated,
or given a comma\-separated list, to deliver to multiple Kindle addresses.
.TP
.BI \-\-smtp\-user " EMAIL"
Override the sender Gmail address from the config file.
.TP
.BI \-\-smtp\-pass " PASSWORD"
Override the SMTP app password from the config file.
.TP
.BI \-\-smtp\-host " HOST"
Override the SMTP host (default: \fIsmtp.gmail.com\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-smtp\-port " PORT"
Override the SMTP port (default: \fI587\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
First-time setup:
.PP
.RS
.B syosetu2epub \-\-setup
.RE
.PP
Scrape and send to your configured Kindle address:
.PP
.RS
.B syosetu2epub n4395il
.RE
.PP
Scrape and save locally without sending:
.PP
.RS
.B syosetu2epub n4395il \-\-local
.RE
.PP
Fetch only the first 20 chapters and send:
.PP
.RS
.B syosetu2epub n4395il \-\-chapters 1\-20
.RE
.PP
Resend an existing EPUB to a different Kindle address:
.PP
.RS
.B syosetu2epub \-\-resend "novel.epub" \-\-send\-to other@kindle.com
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/syosetu2epub/config.json
SMTP credentials and default Kindle email address.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/syosetu2epub/
Per-novel cache directory containing TOC JSON and chapter HTML files.
.SH NOTES
Amazon only delivers documents from approved sender addresses.
Add your Gmail address to the
.B Approved Personal Document Email List
at
.IR "amazon.com \(-> Account \(-> Manage Your Content and Devices \(-> Preferences \(-> Personal Document Settings" .
.PP
Use a Gmail
.I App Password
rather than your account password.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by wolvenspud.
